# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "A note-taking app written in OCaml"
description: """
A desktop note-taking application written entirely in OCaml, both sides of
it. The window is a native one rendered by the system web engine through
owebview; the page inside it is OCaml too, compiled to JavaScript with
js_of_ocaml and driven by ocaml-vdom in the Elm style, so the whole interface
is a pure function of a model.

Browse a directory as a tree, open several files at once as tabs, edit them
and write them back. The two panes are self-contained vdom components that
speak only through their own message types.

The native side answers the page over the webview bridge, and does so on an
Lwt event loop of its own rather than on the UI thread: a slow disk, a network
mount or a large file cannot freeze the window, and several calls interleave
instead of queuing behind each other."""
maintainer: ["frederic.ln.lang@gmail.com"]
authors: ["Frédéric Lang"]
license: "MIT"
tags: ["notes" "editor" "desktop" "webview" "gui" "js_of_ocaml"]
homepage: "https://github.com/korkorran/Sun-notes"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/korkorran/Sun-notes/issues"
depends: [
  "dune" {>= "3.24"}
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "owebview" {>= "0.1.0"}
  "brr"
  "vdom"
  "lwt" {>= "5.3"}
  "js_of_ocaml-compiler"
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "subst"] {dev}
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/korkorran/Sun-notes.git"
x-maintenance-intent: ["(latest)"]
